---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
---

<Layout title="About · Copilot Extensions" description="About Jon's collection of GitHub Copilot extensions.">
  <header style="text-align: center;">
    <h1 style="font-size: clamp(1.75rem, 5vw, 2.5rem); margin: 0 0 0.75rem;">About</h1>
  </header>
  <div style="max-width: 60ch; margin: 0 auto; color: var(--fg);">
    <p>
      This is Jon's collection of <strong>GitHub Copilot extensions</strong>. They
      load from the same place in both the <strong>Copilot app</strong> and the
      <strong>Copilot CLI</strong>. Six are <strong>canvas extensions</strong>
      (interactive side-panel apps in the Copilot app), and three are composable
      <strong>CLI statusline extensions</strong> (<code>pr-statusline</code>,
      <code>issue-statusline</code>, and <code>subagent-statusline</code>) that render
      live pull request, issue, and subagent status pills in the Copilot CLI footer.
    </p>
    <p>
      Every canvas is built on <strong>canvas-kit</strong>, which gives a canvas a
      host-model bridge: <code>ctx.ai(question)</code> for a silent, no-tools answer
      that never adds a turn to the chat, and <code>ctx.askAgent(prompt)</code> to
      hand a tool-capable turn to the main agent.
    </p>
    <p>
      Browse the source on
      <a href="https://github.com/jongio/copilot-extensions" target="_blank" rel="noopener">GitHub</a>.
      Each extension lives in its own self-contained folder under
      <code>extensions/</code>, so any one installs on its own.
    </p>
  </div>
</Layout>
